   "source": [
    "## 1. Introduction & Problem Statement\n",
    "\n",
    "**What is the main objective of this analysis?** The main objective of this analysis is to explore the Electric Vehicle (EV) landscape in Washington State to uncover geographical adoption trends, segment the market based on vehicle performance, and build predictive machine learning models to determine a vehicle's legislative district and its eligibility for Clean Alternative Fuel Vehicle (CAFV) benefits.\n",
    "\n",
    "**What key questions/hypotheses will you explore?** \n",
    "* **Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA):** What are the overarching trends in EV types (BEV vs. PHEV), top manufacturers, and geographic distributions across Washington State?\n",
    "* **Clustering (Segmentation):** The objective of this clustering task is to identify natural groups of electric vehicles based on geographical and performance-related characteristics. Unlike supervised learning, clustering does not require predefined labels. Instead, it discovers hidden structures within the dataset by grouping similar vehicles together.\n",
    "\n",
    "* **Regression:** We aim to predict the **Legislative District** (a discrete integer 1–49 that represents a Washington State electoral zone) from a vehicle's technical and geographical attributes.\n",
    "* **Classification:** The objective is to develop a classification model to predict the **Clean Alternative Fuel Vehicle (CAFV) Eligibility** status of an electric vehicle based on its specifications.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why is this dataset suitable for these questions?** This dataset is highly suitable because it provides a massive, real-world sample size (~135,000 records) of registered EVs. It contains a rich mix of categorical data (Make, Model, City, Utility) ideal for classification and clustering, alongside numeric data (Model Year, Electric Range, Legislative District) necessary for regression. The presence of both geographical and performance-based metrics allows for a comprehensive, multi-faceted machine learning approach.\n",
    "\n",
    "**References** * Washington State Department of Licensing. (2024). *Electric Vehicle Population Data*."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-002",
